# Feature Modules

## 4.1 — OTP & Secure Access

### Flow
```
CPA adds client email
  → system creates client record
  → system starts email monitoring for this email
  → system generates 6-digit OTP
  → OTP sent via Resend
  → client clicks link: /portal?token=xxx
  → system verifies OTP → issues 30-day JWT cookie
  → client accesses portal
```

### OTP generation
```typescript
import crypto from 'crypto'
import bcrypt from 'bcryptjs'

export async function generateOTP(clientId: string) {
  const otp = crypto.randomInt(100000, 999999).toString()
  const hashed = await bcrypt.hash(otp, 10)
  const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000) // 30 days

  await updateClientOTP(clientId, hashed, expiresAt)

  return otp // send this via email, never store plain
}
```

### Key rule
> When CPA adds a client email → auto-trigger OTP send + auto-add to email monitoring list.
> One action, two things happen. CPA does not configure these separately.

